</mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;" color="#000000">
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 2px !important;">
    Powell under pressure
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="Powell under pressure"
  href="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/"
/>
<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>What’s happening? </strong>President Trump escalated his <a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2026/04/15/trump-threatens-to-fire-powell-if-the-fed-chair-doesnt-leave-office-on-his-own.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">fight with Federal Reserve Chair Jerome Powell</a>, saying he could fire Powell if he remains on the Fed’s Board of Governors after his term as chair ends on May 15. Trump linked the threat to a continuing Justice Department probe into cost overruns and management of the Fed’s headquarters renovation, which prosecutors are still pursuing.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Why?</strong> President Trump is escalating the situation for three overlapping reasons: he wants lower interest rates, he wants tighter control over the Fed’s leadership, and Powell’s exit has become entangled in the investigation into the Fed’s headquarters renovation. Trump has long argued the Fed is too cautious on rate cuts, while Powell has resisted political pressure. At the same time, Kevin Warsh’s confirmation to replace Powell is being slowed by Senate opposition tied to that probe.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Probe:</strong> The Justice Department probe focuses on the Federal Reserve’s $2.5B headquarters renovation, which critics say was plagued by cost overruns and poor management. Investigators have examined whether Jerome Powell misled Congress or mishandled the project. But the inquiry has faced setbacks: a judge blocked subpoenas, and prosecutors previously acknowledged they had found no evidence of criminal wrongdoing.</p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

<mj-spacer height="10px" />
