    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;" color="#000000">
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 2px !important;">
    Geelong blaze impact
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="Geelong blaze impact"
  href="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/"
/>
<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>What happened?</strong> A major fire at Viva Energy’s Corio refinery in Geelong, one of only two oil refineries in Australia, has been <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cj40pdw79z9o" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">extinguished after burning for 13 hours</a>. The blaze, reportedly caused by equipment failure, forced the evacuation of dozens of workers, though no injuries were reported. The refinery remains partially operational, but two petrol production units were damaged, raising concerns over fuel output.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Impact: </strong>With Viva’s Geelong refinery supplying about 50% of Victoria’s fuel and 10% nationally, damage to petrol units tightens an already stressed market. Petrol, diesel, and jet fuel output may stay constrained until operations safely recover. The incident also exposes Australia’s vulnerability to relying on just two domestic refineries and imported refined fuel.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Big picture: </strong>Even though the Geelong fire may not trigger an immediate shortage, it exposes the shortcomings of the system. Australia should rely heavily on shipments from Singapore, South Korea, and Malaysia to keep petrol, diesel, and jet fuel flowing. This model puts pressure on the system as the Iran war has resulted in shipping disruptions and market value fluctuations.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong><em>Fact: </em></strong><em>Australia consumes roughly 1.15Mn barrels of oil per day. </em></p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
    <mj-spacer height="10px" />
